                                "example_id": "0bd27c62-60b1-4546-9b2b-14699d07af18",
                                "sense_id": "9ae9dd95-3b90-3989-ab29-8399600454be",
                                "text": "The National Trust reports that 30,000 ash trees on its land will have been felled this year owing to ash dieback. “Dieback” sounds like a gentle, seasonal withdrawal. In fact, ash dieback is a devastating disease caused by a fungus, Hymenoscyphus fraxineus, likely to have been carried into the UK on imported ash saplings in the early part of this century."
                            }
                        ]
